{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Your people — they crush.</b> The reverse. And you say: 'in the heart' — and they crush in deed." "<b>And Your people and Your inheritance</b> — the reverse of 'the wicked'."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {0 "Reading ותאמרו as 'and you say'; the syntax of the whole is compressed and the division between quotation and comment is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:11.186441675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}